# PandaAI Workflow Generator Skill

When the user wants to turn a trading idea into an importable PandaAI workflow JSON file (LiteGraph nodes, links, embedded Python strategy or factor code), use the local skill package.

Preferred local project path:

```text
.cursor/skills/pandaai-workflow-generator
```

Workflow:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/pandaai-workflow-generator/SKILL.md` and follow its Core workflow exactly, including the QBTI hand-off (step 0) and the probe-first rule (step 2a).
2. Read `references/sandbox_restrictions.md` before writing any CodeControl code; the platform statically rejects blacklisted imports and calls.
3. Assemble output only through `scripts/generate_workflow.py` (or `scripts/from_qbti_brief.py` for QBTI briefs); never execute generated strategy code locally.
4. Preserve documented API names, node parameter names, template node ids, and validation limits; do not invent `panda_data` methods.
5. Show the disclaimer from `references/disclaimer_template.md` verbatim before ending the turn.
